course: dictionary
lesson: 11735
title: Words that show how things are done
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Adverbs often tell you how someone does something. «Awkwardly» is one of them. Ask yourself: how did it happen? The adverb gives the answer.
explain: «Mia fell awkwardly off the bike and grazed her knee.» The fall was not smooth or easy, so awkwardly means in a clumsy way. Check it by swapping in a word like clumsily. The sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Sam stood awkwardly at the front of the class, not knowing what to say.» Nobody is hurt here. The clues are not knowing what to say and standing at the front, so awkwardly means in an embarrassed or uncomfortable way. Swap in nervously and see if it still fits.
explain: Awkwardly can also describe things. «The box was awkwardly shaped, so it was hard to carry.» The box was hard to hold because of its shape, so awkwardly means in a way that is hard to handle.
fact: Awkwardly is an adverb. It tells you how something is done.
fact: Awkwardly means in a clumsy way that is not smooth or easy.
fact: Awkwardly can also mean in an embarrassed or uncomfortable way.
fact: Awkwardly can describe something that is hard to handle or badly placed.
fact: In safety talk, «landed awkwardly» means landed badly and could lead to an injury.
exercise: «Mia fell awkwardly off the bike.» What does awkwardly tell you about the fall? | *In a clumsy way that was not smooth | On purpose to show off | In a happy, bouncy way | Very slowly and carefully
exercise: «Sam stood awkwardly at the front of the class, not knowing what to say.» What does awkwardly show? | *He felt embarrassed and uncomfortable | He was fast asleep | He was very proud of himself | He was dancing with joy
exercise: «The box was awkwardly shaped, so it was hard to carry.» What made the box hard to carry? | It had a bright red lid | It was very light | It was made of paper | *Its awkward shape
test: «Dad laughed awkwardly when he dropped the cake on the floor.» What does awkwardly suggest? | He was delighted by the mess | He was very angry | *He felt embarrassed | He had just won a prize
test: «The puppy ran awkwardly across the wet kitchen floor.» Which word is the adverb? | kitchen | *awkwardly | puppy | floor
exam: Lucy says, «I landed awkwardly, so my ankle hurts.» What does landed awkwardly mean? | Landed on her feet in a dance | Landed first in the race | *Landed badly and could be hurt | Landed very softly on a mat
